Every post on this blog is written in Markdown — a lightweight formatting syntax that keeps you focused on the words instead of the markup. This sample post doubles as a quick reference.

# The essentials

Headings start with `#`, emphasis uses asterisks, and lists are just dashes or numbers:

- *italic* text uses one asterisk
- **bold** text uses two
- [links](https://www.platformos.com) are square brackets followed by parentheses

# Quotes and code

Blockquotes work the way you would expect:

> Good writing is rewriting. Publish, read it again, improve it.

Inline `code` uses backticks, and fenced blocks get syntax highlighting automatically:

```liquid
{% raw %}{% liquid
  function posts = 'modules/blog/queries/blog_posts/search', per_page: 10
  assign featured = posts.results.first
%}{% endraw %}
```

# Images and more

Images use the link syntax with a leading exclamation mark. When you add an image through the post editor, it is uploaded to the platformOS CDN and the Markdown is generated for you.

That is genuinely all you need to publish well-formatted articles. Open this post in the admin editor to see the source side by side with the result.
