As your blog grows, tags keep it navigable. This post explains how tags work on the platformOS Blog and how to use them well.

# How tags work

Each post can carry any number of tags. The tags you configure in **Blog Settings → Tags filter** appear as the category chips on the home page, and every tag on a post links to a filtered listing of related articles.

# A few guidelines

1. **Keep the list short.** Five to eight tags cover most blogs; more than that and readers stop using them.
1. **Prefer topics over types.** "design" and "tutorials" age better than "misc" or "news".
1. **Be consistent.** Pick a casing and stick to it — tags are matched exactly.
1. **Revisit occasionally.** If a tag has only one post after months of writing, fold it into a broader one.

# Categories on the home page

The chips at the top of the post list come straight from your settings, so the navigation always reflects the topics you actually write about. Readers can jump between categories without leaving the page flow, and the RSS feed keeps working across all of them.
