The Blog Settings page in the Dashboard is small on purpose — a handful of options that shape the whole site. Here is what each one does.

# Identity

- **Title and subtitle** render in the hero on the home page and set the browser title. Keep the subtitle to one sentence; it doubles as your blog's elevator pitch.
- **Hero image** sits behind the title. Wide, calm images work best — the layout adds a dark overlay so white text stays readable on anything.

# Content

- **Tags filter** defines the categories offered on the home page and in the post editor.
- **Posts** are managed on their own pages — writing, editing and scheduling all happen in the post form, where you can also upload a hero image per post.

# Reach

- **Social media links** (Facebook, X, Instagram, LinkedIn) show up as icons in the footer.
- **Facebook app id** enables the comments block under every post. Leave it empty and the blog simply skips comments.
- The **RSS feed** at `/blog/rss.rss` is always on, so readers can subscribe from day one.

Change a setting, refresh the home page, and you will see the effect immediately — there is no separate publish step for configuration.
