Your blog ships production-ready. Before you announce it, run through this short checklist to make the most of what is already built in.

# Before you hit publish

1. **Replace the sample content.** Unpublish or delete these starter posts once you have a few of your own.
1. **Set your title and subtitle.** They appear in the hero, the browser tab and search results.
1. **Add your social links.** The footer icons and the share buttons under each post are wired up as soon as the links are set.

# SEO comes standard

Every post renders its title and excerpt as meta tags, slugs are clean and human-readable, and category pages have stable URLs you can link to from anywhere. Publishing dates are real `time` elements, which search engines read directly.

# Give readers a way to stay

The RSS feed at `/blog/rss.rss` updates automatically with every published post. Add the link wherever your audience lives — a newsletter footer, a community channel, your product's changelog page.

# Measure what matters

Connect Google Analytics from the Dashboard to see which topics resonate. Combined with tags, a month of data usually tells you exactly what to write next.

That is the whole launch. Write the next post — that is the part only you can do.
